---
// The Workload case study: opens over the page from "Case study" under the Workload
// card (scripts/case-study.ts). Text on the left in three parts, one open at a time;
// on the right the card in its studio frame, on its own and as the pair.
import { WorkloadCase } from "./islands/WeeklyUsageIsland.tsx"

const PARTS = [
    {
        title: "The idea",
        text: "Each model gets its own agent, with its own chat history and its own skills. A project is selected behind the scenes, and every agent works on it at the same time. You give them tasks at once, move between them easily, and see your weekly usage at a glance.",
    },
    {
        title: "The problem",
        text: [
            "I work with Claude every day and switch models depending on the task: Sonnet when I need copy, Opus for more advanced work. But when I switch, it all still happens in the same chat.",
            "Every prompt costs tokens, so you want to be conscious of writing the right prompts and picking the right model, to spend as few as possible. That’s why usage is easy to see, and why each agent suggests its next prompt: it steers you the right way, instead of wasting tokens on the wrong ones.",
        ],
    },
    {
        title: "The challenge",
        text: [
            "The hardest part was the layout of the agents. In Figma I tried a few options, including a 2x2 grid instead of a scrollable list. Everything fit on one screen, but with so much going on at once it was harder to take in.",
            "The list also does something the grid can’t: it’s ordered by usage, so the agent using the most always sits on top and you see it first. A grid has no clear top, so that ordering gets lost. And with a list, an agent has room to open in one smooth motion, without pushing the others around.",
        ],
    },
]
---

<dialog class="case" id="case-workload" aria-labelledby="case-workload-title">
    <div class="case-sheet">
        <div class="case-text">
            <button class="case-back" type="button" data-case-close>Back</button>
            <h2 class="case-title" id="case-workload-title">Workload</h2>
            <p class="case-sub">A home for a team of AI agents. Concept, 2026.</p>
            <div class="case-parts">
                {PARTS.map((p, i) => (
                    <section class:list={["case-part", { "is-open": i === 0 }]}>
                        <h3>
                            <button class="case-part-btn" type="button" aria-expanded={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"} data-case-part>
                                {p.title}
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div class="case-part-body">
                            <div>
                                {[p.text].flat().map((para) => (
                                    <p>{para}</p>
                                ))}
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                ))}
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-media">
            <div class="case-frame"><WorkloadCase client:visible view="single" /></div>
            <div class="case-frame"><WorkloadCase client:visible view="pair" /></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</dialog>
